db/ref 17592186311099} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9201af61-5396-5015-9da5-5672febbfbae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9201af61-5396-5015-9da5-5672febbfbae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309915} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ec3e5c-8ef3-5870-a471-f6da36149650" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8513caf0-a922-5e88-ab45-1bb4f8fa5345" :question/math-academy-id "q-335310" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=1-2y+z,\\, && y(0)=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=2+x-w,\\, && z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′} &=yz,\\, && w(0)=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈$\n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nFirst, because the initial conditions are $y(0)=0,$ $z(0)=1,$ and $w(0)=2,$ we place $y=0,$ $z=1,$ and $w=2$ in the table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  | $2$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},{z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =1-2y+z \\\\  & =1-2\\cdot 0+1 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2+x-w \\\\  & =2+0-2 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ {w}^{′} & =yz \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |  | $2$ | $0$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0 \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+1=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+0=1 \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=2+0=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  | $2$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈1,$\n$z\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈1,$\nand\n$w\\,(\\frac{1}{2})≈2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "493c1f47-258d-5c5a-b2e5-55208f1a0a9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "493c1f47-258d-5c5a-b2e5-55208f1a0a9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309309} :answer-field/id #uuid "005eaf4b-c8ef-5935-81ce-a3c20b5c14c8" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310792} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8482877-2f97-5697-ab88-8c95b44a3f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8482877-2f97-5697-ab88-8c95b44a3f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310593} :answer-field/id #uuid "172e5570-347e-5023-a6de-7d0a6554baf5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a67d665-7c06-55ce-86af-b1b38ff3f2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a67d665-7c06-55ce-86af-b1b38ff3f2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309994} :answer-field/id #uuid "3434226d-76f8-50e2-b9f3-bf9085cf8151" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310931} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f43fda5d-6cdc-5267-8a31-56854df651af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f43fda5d-6cdc-5267-8a31-56854df651af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310689} :answer-field/id #uuid "7590d484-35e7-5539-8b34-5ea9c2ef0851" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1c05d8b-7204-5dc7-96ac-9c4ed759b124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c05d8b-7204-5dc7-96ac-9c4ed759b124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310307} :answer-field/id #uuid "d646e1ee-1b8c-51e7-94ee-9f5f6960ac71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef7fe7bd-52ce-5d06-87c9-70acf329ceea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef7fe7bd-52ce-5d06-87c9-70acf329ceea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310656} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb33fbea-9b4d-5fe1-8bba-0866d2cc6a9a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4387698-260c-5af9-836c-bad394d949ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-335318" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=1+x-2y+3z,\\, && y(0)=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=2y-w,\\, && z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′} &=-x+yz,\\, && w(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4}?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈$\n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Euler's method approximates the solution of an initial value problem containing a system of ODEs by applying the update rule component-wise to each equation.\n\nFirst, because the initial conditions are $y(0)=0,$ $z(0)=1,$ and $w(0)=1,$ we place $y=0,$ $z=1,$ and $w=1$ in the table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{′},{z}^{′},$ and ${w}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =1+x-2y+3z \\\\  & =1+0-2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2y-w \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0-1 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {w}^{′} & =-x+yz \\\\  & =-0+0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $4$ |  | $1$ | $-1$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |  |\n\nFinally, we compute $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ Δw & ={w}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ $z,$ and $w$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ $Δz$ to $z,$ and $Δw$ to $w,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=0+1=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+(-\\frac{1}{4})=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {w}_{\\text{new}} & =w+Δw=1+0=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |  |  | $\\frac{3}{4}$ |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈1,$\n$z\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈\\frac{3}{4},$\nand\n$w\\,(\\frac{1}{4})≈1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3368270-e613-5878-b19f-40a2c3459edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3368270-e613-5878-b19f-40a2c3459edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310313} :answer-field/id #uuid "2149ed14-bfec-5df3-ba48-f4bb23b4243f" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7f3f