-e3a4-5348-9b23-bad945e1873f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309716} :answer-field/id #uuid "be3815c6-86ba-5b1b-8cae-ec097bb7034c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "172bcc96-0511-568d-93d5-02dd842fe19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308928} {:answer/id #uuid "4f22f86e-db07-50a9-ba4f-3e7c66bc3bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309349} {:answer/id #uuid "70719a3e-27ba-591a-8f36-1481d2e108a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309620} {:answer/id #uuid "e3e67a54-a1b1-5bf1-8639-de55c1eb37ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310568} {:answer/id #uuid "e8704c4a-06a4-5550-844c-30942e45edc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310595} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7424e5-fcc6-5a10-9795-fd29c7199ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3e67a54-a1b1-5bf1-8639-de55c1eb37ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310568} :answer-field/id #uuid "d40fb636-0bef-5c56-b7fe-be072b8cced7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ee0e09f-2dc3-5d79-8a91-2daee5f981be" :question/math-academy-id "q-335462" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x})$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,\\frac{1}{x}=O(1)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines  \n{{field-4}}  \nand  \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}),\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,(\\frac{1}{x}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{x}=O(1).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines   $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and $\\text{the transitive property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143783ba-f667-5508-b07b-b9fa079bbea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308897} {:answer/id #uuid "1c468251-7329-5d23-9077-e19b8e8726bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308967} {:answer/id #uuid "60059968-1161-56a5-a638-36fd6b700958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309471} {:answer/id #uuid "608c36e3-b013-5cae-8a3d-d4b915200e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309481} {:answer/id #uuid "89337a20-49e6-5768-9a11-333a7f53f3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309826} {:answer/id #uuid "eef5ead3-fd02-5d0d-9d2c-f712b842ae71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310652}] :answer-field/correct 